      "side": 1,
      "message": "The PrivateAddrssCoordinator is to generate an random unused LinkAddress. Change 192.168.A.B/24 to 192.168.A.B to avoid confusing with prefix length.\nIn the example of commit message, 192.168.A.B, A is 8 bits sub prefix from 192.168.0.0/16 and B is 8 bits sub address.\n\nThus A, B for private LinkAddress with /24 prefix length would be:\n10.0.0.0/8    -\u003e 10.A(16 bits 0x0000 ~ 0xFFFF).B(8 bits)\nB 172.16.0.0/12 -\u003e 172.A(0x1000 ~ 0x1FFF).B(8 bits)\n192.168.0.0/16 -\u003e 192.168.A(8 bits).B(8 bits)",
